This is true, of course.  I did skip over the whole issue of whether
gain energy itself is balanced in favor of discussing whether there
should be more Pw recharge at all.  But as a general principle, I agree.

> I also agree with Derek's observation that mana recharge should not be
> made -too- common.  But potions of gain energy are rare (and have
> special mixing applications too), and one-use only, so I would have no
> objections to them giving a full power recharge and have charging be
> downgraded somewhat (although, as a one-use item, it should still have
> a significant effect).

The "full power recharge" is where it starts to cause problems, though.

A priest who reaches level 30 gets about 400-500 Pw straight up, _simply_
from having such a high Wisdom at XL1.  That's a lot.  Allowing a single
potion of gain energy to reload all that is too strong without
artificially over-limiting the frequency of gain energy potions... and
that violates the long-ago-discussed principle of "if you have a thing
that breaks the game, making it happen very rarely doesn't fix it, it
just makes it random."

Right now the primary purpose of the potion of gain energy appears to be
increasing the user's _maximum_ Pw, and the reloading of existing Pw is
simply a side effect.  Changing the recharging effect to, say, be worth 
about 100Pw or so wouldn't be bad at all; it'd make it very useful
for the semi-caster roles, and not _un_useful for the casters.  At the
moment, I'm not sure I've ever used one for _anything_ other than
alchemy.

